hello,

I've restarted my annotated NetHack code project and one of the problems 
is that what we are calling items in NetHack are called objects in the 
code. These objects in the code contain also such objects as venoms, 
unpaid used items and items that are currently in use, whisch are not 
items per se.

So my question is: What should I call these in my annotations: objects 
or items?

The code also has an array objects[] which doesn't contain any objects 
at all but the object types. So objects array has an entry for a dagger, 
but all of those lovely daggers we so fondly toss around are not 
contained in this arraay objects[] but instead in linked lists that 
tells if they are in the heros inventory, traveling through the air 
towards an enemy (or whatever if it misses), on the floor where they 
landed, buried in the ice that was generated by the blue dragon, picked 
up by an uffish orc, dropped down the stairs to a lower level or in our 
BoH. If for some reason you are buying them, instead of letting your pet 
steal them, they are yet on other list. But they are never on any array.

So what would you suggest? All items, all objects or depending on what 
the code is doing?

